CAT = "cpafarRevenue"; SEG = "REV"
Q = [
("The first step of the ASC 606 five-step revenue model is to:",
 "Identify the contract", ["Identify the obligations", "Set the transaction price", "Allocate the price"],
 "The steps are: identify the contract, identify the performance obligations, determine the transaction price, allocate it, and recognize revenue as each obligation is satisfied."),
("A company sells a device with a year of support for $900. Standalone selling prices are $800 for the device and $200 for the support. Revenue allocated to the device is:",
 "$720", ["$800", "$700", "$450"],
 "The price is allocated by relative standalone selling price: $900 x $800 / $1,000 = $720. Giving the support its full $200 and the device the rest ($700) is a residual approach that does not apply here."),
("A promised good is a separate performance obligation when it is:",
 "Distinct and separately identifiable", ["Priced on a separate invoice", "Delivered in a separate month", "Listed in a separate clause"],
 "A good is distinct if the customer can benefit from it on its own or with readily available resources and the promise is separately identifiable in the contract. Invoicing and timing do not decide it."),
("Variable consideration is included in the transaction price only to the extent that:",
 "It is probable no significant reversal occurs", ["It is more likely than not to be earned in full", "It is certain to be collected in cash", "It is reasonably possible to be earned"],
 "The constraint includes variable consideration only to the extent it is probable that a significant reversal of cumulative revenue will not occur when the uncertainty resolves."),
("Which condition means revenue is recognized over time rather than at a point in time?",
 "Customer consumes benefits as performed", ["Customer pays half the price upfront", "Contract runs for over a year", "Seller sends a bill each month"],
 "One of the ASC 606 over-time criteria is that the customer simultaneously receives and consumes the benefits as the entity performs, as in a cleaning service. Billing and payment terms do not decide it."),
("A contractor's price is $2,000,000 and its total estimated cost is $1,500,000. Costs incurred to date are $600,000. Using a cost-to-cost input method, revenue to date is:",
 "$800,000", ["$600,000", "$1,200,000", "$200,000"],
 "Progress is $600,000 / $1,500,000 = 40%, and 40% x $2,000,000 = $800,000. $200,000 is the gross profit to date, not revenue."),
("An online platform arranges hotel stays but never controls the rooms. It recognizes revenue equal to:",
 "Its net fee or commission", ["The full room price charged", "The room price less taxes", "Nothing until the guest leaves"],
 "An agent that arranges for another party to provide the service recognizes revenue as the net fee it keeps. A principal that controls the service before transfer reports the gross amount."),
("A salesperson earns a $9,000 commission for signing a three-year service contract that the company expects to recover. The commission is:",
 "Capitalized and amortized", ["Expensed when it is paid", "Capitalized, never amortized", "Netted against revenue"],
 "Incremental costs of obtaining a contract are capitalized when expected to be recovered and amortized as the services transfer. Expensing is a practical expedient only when amortization would be one year or less."),
("A consignor ships goods to a consignee who sells them to end customers. The consignor recognizes revenue:",
 "When the consignee sells them", ["When it ships them out", "When the consignee pays", "At the end of each reporting month"],
 "In a consignment the consignee does not obtain control of the goods, so the consignor recognizes revenue when control passes to the end customer."),
("A company delivers equipment today for a single payment of $121,000 due in two years. The financing component is significant and the discount rate is 10%. Revenue at delivery is:",
 "$100,000", ["$121,000", "$110,000", "$90,000"],
 "With a significant financing component, revenue is the cash selling price: $121,000 / 1.1^2 = $100,000. The $21,000 is interest income over the two years."),
("A retailer gives customers loyalty points that are a material right for future purchases. When it makes a sale, the retailer:",
 "Defers part of the price to the points", ["Records all of the price now", "Expenses the expected cost of points", "Records the points as a liability at cost"],
 "Points that give a material right are a separate performance obligation, so part of the transaction price is allocated to them and recognized when they are redeemed or expire."),
("A not-for-profit receives an unconditional pledge of $50,000 payable next year. It records:",
 "Revenue now, with donor restriction", ["Revenue when the cash arrives", "Revenue now, without restriction", "A refundable advance from the donor"],
 "An unconditional promise to give is recognized when received. Payment in a later period implies a time restriction, so it is reported with donor restrictions."),
("A donor promises a not-for-profit $100,000 only if the charity raises a matching $100,000 by year-end, otherwise the donor owes nothing. The charity recognizes the contribution:",
 "When the match is raised", ["When the promise is made", "Evenly over the year", "When the donor sends the cash"],
 "A promise with a barrier and a right of release is conditional. It is recognized only when the barrier is overcome, here when the matching funds are raised."),
("Which contributed service does a not-for-profit recognize as revenue?",
 "An electrician rewiring the building", ["Volunteers stuffing donation envelopes", "Board members at monthly meetings", "Volunteers greeting museum visitors"],
 "Contributed services are recognized only if they create or enhance nonfinancial assets or need specialized skills that would otherwise be purchased. General volunteer work does not qualify."),
("A charity receives cash from a donor, with instructions to pass it to a named shelter, and has no variance power. The charity records:",
 "A liability to the shelter", ["Contribution revenue, no restriction", "Restricted contribution revenue", "Deferred revenue"],
 "An entity acting as an agent or intermediary with no variance power does not have a contribution. It records the asset and a matching liability to the beneficiary."),
("A not-for-profit receives donated land with a fair value of $300,000. The donor paid $120,000 for it. Contribution revenue is:",
 "$300,000", ["$120,000", "$180,000", "$0"],
 "Contributed nonfinancial assets are recognized at fair value when received. The donor's cost does not matter."),
]
